# .env.example — every env var documented, values blank.
#
# CHANGE: list the repo's real env vars with a one-line description each.
#
# DO NOT CHANGE:
# - Values stay BLANK here; real values live in the shell env, never in
#   files. .env is copied from this file by `make setup` and loaded ONLY
#   by run-type targets (`uv run --env-file .env`) — real env wins over
#   file values (that's --env-file precedence, which shell sourcing does
#   NOT have: `set -a; . ./.env` clobbers real vars with blank values).
# - Never commit API keys here or anywhere.

# The app reads values from the real environment (os.environ) — .env is a
# dev convenience, not a runtime artifact.
# EXAMPLE_VAR=          # one-line description of what this does

# LLM Provider — set these to wherever you route AI calls.
# Default: Cloudflare AI Gateway (OpenCode → DeepSeek fallback).
# Fork: point at your own provider.
# Text model: dynamic/fallback2. Vision model: dynamic/image.
OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://gateway.ai.cloudflare.com/v1/e21a5be58ac1e8f7d5619539feb2dc3d/default/compat
OPENAI_API_KEY=
